// shiftable.storyarc
// part of Arcturus, a programming language and compiler for the Infocom Z-machine.
// Copyright (c) 2026, Stefan Vogt.
// https://github.com/ByteProject/Arcturus
//
// A showcase for shiftable (docs/01 chapter 12): a thing marked
// `shiftable` can be pushed through an exit, and the player goes with
// it: doors are respected exactly as walking respects them, the arrival
// is the same a walk gets, and the thing is there when the room is
// described. Anything unmarked answers that it will not shift, and a
// game with nothing shiftable pays nothing for any of this. Compile
// and run:
//
//   arcc examples/features/shiftable.storyarc -o shiftable.z5
//   frotz shiftable.z5
//
// Try, in order:
//   push barrel north     the barrel rolls into the warehouse, you follow
//   look                  the barrel is here, listed like anything else
//   push barrel east      no exit that way: refused like a walk would be
//   push barrel south     back out to the dock, barrel first
//   push crane north      the crane is not shiftable: it will not budge
//   push barrel up        onto the ramp? an exit is an exit

game
    title  "The Tar Barrel"
    headline "A shiftable showcase"
    author "Stefan Vogt"
    start  dock

summon.statusline

room dock
    name "The Dock"
    desc "Salt wind and gull argument. A warehouse stands north, and a
          loading ramp climbs to its roof."
    north warehouse
    up ramp

room warehouse
    name "The Warehouse"
    desc "Stacked crates and the smell of tar. The dock lies south."
    south dock

room ramp
    name "The Loading Ramp"
    desc "A plank ramp with a view of grey water. The dock is below."
    down dock

thing barrel in dock
    name "tar barrel"
    words barrel, tar
    shiftable
    desc "Heavy, but round: the docker's compromise."

thing crane in dock
    name "loading crane"
    words crane, loading
    fixed
    desc "Bolted through the planking into bedrock, probably."
